<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113568" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρᾰγωγ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leading, guiding,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἀρχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					8.464
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Egypt</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst., <i>leader, guide,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχει . . χ. τὸν πλοῦτον ὁ γέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					127
				</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				13.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.794d
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ βίου τυφλὴ χ.</span> (of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τύχη</span>), ib.<i><span class="en">
				98b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖς ἕπεσθαι χειραγωγοῖς ἡγούμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Or.</u>
					61.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
